    "citation": "Mehlqvist, K., Wigforss-Lange, J. & Vajda, V. 2015. A palynological study from Sweden reveals stable terrestrial environments during Late Silurian extreme marine conditions. Earth and Environmental Science Transactions of the Royal Society of Edinburgh 105, 149–158.",
    "language": "English",
    "reports_window_spores": true,
    "comment": "The study reports 20 samples from a composite Klinta outcrop section. Table I gives percentages for combined morphotaxa as well as individual taxa. Figure 7 illustrates selected taxa but does not identify the samples containing the illustrated specimens; illustrated flags below identify illustrated taxa, not confirmed specimens from each sample. Independent conodont and chitinozoan ages support the spore-based Ludlow age. The paper compares its results with earlier drillcore studies by Mehlqvist et al. (2012, 2014); those comparisons are not new sample records."
